#### keeps `_` bound to the outer tuple when a template slot calls a plain function

- Verify: keeps `_` bound to the outer tuple when a template slot calls a plain function


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: keeps `_` bound to the outer tuple when a template slot calls a plain function")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val pairs = [("count", 1), ("ready", 2)]
val result = pairs.map("{_.0}: {double_val(_.1)}")
expect result == ["count: 2", "ready: 4"]
```

</details>

#### keeps `_` bound to the outer tuple when a template slot calls a method (type_mapper map_struct shape)

- Verify: keeps `_` bound to the outer tuple when a template slot calls a method (type_mapper map_struct shape)


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 6 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: keeps `_` bound to the outer tuple when a template slot calls a method (type_mapper map_struct shape)")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val pairs = [("count", 1), ("ready", 2)]
val doubler = Doubler.create()
val result = pairs.map("{_.0}: {doubler.apply(_.1)}")
expect result == ["count: 2", "ready: 4"]
```

